%% Multi-agent orchestration, with the cost shown honestly.
%% Each hop is a new contract, a new failure point, and more latency.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Goal
    participant Orch as Orchestrator
    participant Budget
    participant Res as Researcher
    participant Rev as Reviewer
    participant Human

    Goal->>Orch: "what evidence does policy require for a write"
    Orch->>Budget: charge_step()
    Budget-->>Orch: within limits

    Orch->>Res: __call__(task) - typed contract
    Res-->>Orch: Finding(summary, evidence, confidence)
    Note right of Res
      A typed result with evidence is what
      makes delegation auditable. Free prose
      forces the parent to trust it blindly.
    end Note

    alt no evidence returned
        Orch-->>Human: escalate, do not guess
    else evidence found
        Orch->>Budget: charge_step() + charge_tool_call()
        Orch->>Rev: __call__(task, finding)
        Rev-->>Orch: Finding(accepted or rejected)

        alt reviewer rejects
            Orch->>Human: needs_human = true
        else accepted and confidence >= threshold
            Orch-->>Goal: answer with confidence
        end
    end

    Note over Orch,Rev
      Start with ONE agent and several tools.
      Add an agent only when you need a different
      permission set, a different context window,
      or an independent judgement - not because
      the prompt got long.
    end Note